WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.930
- [Kelly Clarkson] You're about to be a

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.320
part of a groundbreaking, like

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.239
new Broadway show, right?
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:04.239 --> 00:00:05.646
- [Kandi Burruss] Yessss, I'm so excited!

00:00:05.646 --> 00:00:07.170
- That's a lot of work!

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.810
- Yes! So, the show is called,
Thoughts of a Colored Man.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.643
- Yeah.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.710
- And it's a groundbreaking
show because this is the first

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.030
time ever that seven black
men, an all black cast,

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.610
starring on Broadway with a director who,

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.283
black director, black writer.

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:24.411
- Yeah, African-American
everything, I love that.

00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:26.420
- Black producer,
African-American everything!

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.745
The thing about it is, you
know, for so, so many years,

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:30.578
you know,

00:00:30.578 --> 00:00:33.260
we didn't see enough diversity
on Broadway and now we're

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.040
coming back and we bring in
such spice to diversity when

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:36.873
Broadway is coming back.

00:00:36.873 --> 00:00:37.706
- Yeah.

00:00:37.706 --> 00:00:42.706
- It's an amazing show
mixing, spoken word with,

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:43.940
it's just amazing.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.550
You just have to see it to see
black men in that light where

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.070
they're bringing such greatness
to the theater and I'm

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:50.960
excited about it.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.030
- Yeah, and they're all
different, you said there's seven

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:52.863
different lives, right?

00:00:52.863 --> 00:00:55.996
- Yes, well, they're different,
bringing different emotions.

00:00:55.996 --> 00:00:56.829
- Ooh!

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:58.430
- So we'll see them in a way
that you've never seen before,

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:01.710
starring some amazing actors.
I'm a producer on the show.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.065
A lot of people think
that I'm in the show,

00:01:04.065 --> 00:01:05.490
I'm a producer on the show.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.610
And so for me to be behind the scenes,

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.840
working on a show like this
on Broadway in this way,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.220
when this is the first time
Broadway has ever shut down for

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.053
as long as it did.

00:01:16.053 --> 00:01:16.886
- Yeah.

00:01:16.886 --> 00:01:18.640
- So to be able to come back and come in,

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.760
and I actually be a part
of a show that's coming,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.810
bringing Broadway back to life.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:23.643
- Yeah.

00:01:23.643 --> 00:01:24.476
- I'm just so excited.

00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:26.660
I really hope that everybody
chooses to come and hang out

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:27.920
with us and see the show.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.940
It's going to be amazing

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.299
- I think everyone.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:31.460
- We start in October.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.310
- Everyone's dying to come
back and see the show.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.640
I literally have already been
to like two, like concert.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.610
I'm like, and I'm doing it
safely, but I'm just like,

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.110
I need a life.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.960
Like we want our lives up,
we want to be entertained.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.843
And especially coming to New York.

00:01:43.843 --> 00:01:46.953
- Listen, New York is
the place for theater.

00:01:46.953 --> 00:01:47.786
- For the arts, yeah.

00:01:47.786 --> 00:01:50.550
- And musicals, and arts, and you know,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.940
it was kinda sad to see,

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.008
you know, all the shows have
to shut down for so long.

00:01:55.008 --> 00:01:55.841
- Yeah.

00:01:55.841 --> 00:02:00.560
- So I'm just so happy that
we're able to bring life back to

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.080
the theater world again.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.060
- It's kinda cool too though,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.760
because then it reminds
us how great we had it.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.050
We didn't even know how lucky
we were to see so many shows,

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.190
whatever you want to do
at the same, you know,

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.040
at the tip of your fingers,
like it's always all here,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.890
and then it all went away and
you were like, wait a minute.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.900
Like we needed that.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.733
- Yes!

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:16.200
- We didn't realize how,
especially a city like this.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.703
I'm so stoked for you.
Congratulations, That's so cool.

00:02:18.703 --> 00:02:19.536
- Thank you!

00:02:19.536 --> 00:02:21.596
- Yeah, It's so, so, so cool.

00:02:21.596 --> 00:02:23.730
So the last time you
were here, we were about,

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.020
you were about to welcome a
new daughter. So how is she.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:26.860
- Blaze?

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.220
- Yeah. Which is such a great name,

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.720
but you're kind of setting
yourself up for like a

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:30.880
firecracker.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.985
- She's a firecracker!

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.818
(both laughing)

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:33.651
- Her name represents her well.

00:02:33.651 --> 00:02:34.484
- I know, I was like. (laughs)

00:02:34.484 --> 00:02:39.250
- Listen, she is such a
sweetheart, but at the same time,

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.540
she's so feisty.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.373
- Mine is too.

00:02:41.373 --> 00:02:43.480
- And so funny, like with
Blaze, okay, she makes

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.660
these faces, right?

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.680
- Yeah.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.480
- Like me, I make, everybody knows

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.313
- Expressive, yep.

00:02:48.313 --> 00:02:50.420
- She's very expressive, but you know,

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.310
I had to do this thing with
her because she just does what

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.143
she wants to do.

00:02:53.143 --> 00:02:56.110
And so I had to get to get in
her face and say stop it right

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.030
now. So now what she does
to me is when she's mad,

00:02:59.030 --> 00:02:59.863
she's like.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.970
- Oh my gosh. And so young
and doing that already.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.740
- Yes! Frowning up at me, and telling me.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.220
- Good luck. (claps)

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.260
So here's the face I want
to talk about though.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.376
Have you ever felt yourself
having your mom's face?

00:03:13.376 --> 00:03:16.190
Like you can feel that you
have your mom's face with your

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.550
child when you're like angry
or something. I'm like,

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.620
oh my God, that was my mom.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.380
- Well, my mom, definitely
makes faces. So I think it's,

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.070
it's a generational
thing, we can't help it.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.953
- Yeah, yeah, we're all expressive.

